From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: use HTTPS for VideoLAN download mirrors

Current GitHub-hosted builds repeatedly fail while fetching contrib tarballs
from `downloads.videolan.org` over plain HTTP:

  curl: (28) Failed to connect to downloads.videolan.org port 80

This now affects multiple platform families once they source-build contribs
(Android after the GLES2 link fix, Windows x86_64 after disabling the mismatched
prebuilt bundle). Switch VLC's built-in VideoLAN archive roots to HTTPS so the
same fetch rules continue to work without relying on port 80.
---
 contrib/src/main.mak | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/contrib/src/main.mak b/contrib/src/main.mak
index a4a930d..a3be5c0 100644
--- a/contrib/src/main.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/main.mak
@@ -20,8 +20,8 @@ VPATH := $(TARBALLS)
 # Common download locations
 GNU ?= http://ftpmirror.gnu.org/gnu
 SF := https://netcologne.dl.sourceforge.net/
-VIDEOLAN := http://downloads.videolan.org/pub/videolan
-CONTRIB_VIDEOLAN := http://downloads.videolan.org/pub/contrib
+VIDEOLAN := https://downloads.videolan.org/pub/videolan
+CONTRIB_VIDEOLAN := https://downloads.videolan.org/pub/contrib
 GITHUB := https://github.com/
 GNUGPG := https://www.gnupg.org/ftp/gcrypt
 XIPH := https://ftp.osuosl.org/pub/xiph/releases
